Prefixes make big and small numbers easier:
• mega (M) = {1000000}
• kilo (k) = {1000}
• centi (c) = {1} ÷ {100}
• milli (m) = {1} ÷ {1000}
• micro (µ) = {1} ÷ {1000000}
So {3.2} km = {3200} m, and {450} mm = {0.45} m. To change to a smaller unit the number gets bigger, and the other way round.
